I hold the chocolate up to the camera.
"This is a German brand," I explain.
Sofia sees the chocolate on the screen.
"Is a big supermarket nearby?" she asks.
I shake my head.
"No," I answer.
"Supermarkets are closed today."
"Who sells chocolate on Sunday?" Mom asks.
"A small kiosk sells chocolate," I say.
"That is a Späti."
"A Späti is right around the corner here."
"That is a real Berlin specialty."
Diego laughs into the camera.
"My smart sister always finds chocolate," my brother says.
"Yes," I joke.
"My chocolate is very important!"
I open the package.
I eat a piece of chocolate.
My family laughs with me.
The morning in Mexico and my afternoon in Berlin are very nice.
